# Advisories ignored for sandbox-libkrun/Cargo.lock only (see .github/workflows/rust-security-audit.yml).
#
# zstd 0.13 / zstd-safe 7 come from msb_krun_vmm, whose latest release (0.1.42)
# still requires zstd ^0.13 (upstream fix: libkrun/libkrun#948). It uses zstd only on
# x86_64, to decompress the bundled kernel image (zstd::stream::copy_decode), which
# reaches none of the vulnerable code. Drop all three when msb_krun moves to
# zstd 0.14.
#
# Affects only raw::Encoder::with_context and raw::Decoder::with_context, which
# borrow a context across streams. copy_decode builds its own context.
RUSTSEC-2026-0391
# Affects only Seekable::decompress (the `seekable` feature, not enabled).
RUSTSEC-2026-0398
# Affects only zstd::stream::write::Decoder. The advisory states that
# read::Decoder, decode_all and the bulk API (copy_decode reads through
# read::Decoder) are unaffected.
RUSTSEC-2026-0403
